From: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Nov 2025 11:27:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: use dedicated MT7990 TX-free ring for WED

Current mt76 routes MT7990 TX-free notifications through dedicated WFDMA
RX ring 6 and interrupt bit 14.  Point WED at the same ring and interrupt,
so that it receives the device's completion notifications.  The MT7996
TXFREE0 and MT7992 WA-ring mappings are unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/671c2416d6219beb19abbb05709e418a6363be62/autobuild/unified/filogic/mac80211/25.12/files/package/kernel/mt76/patches/0048-mtk-mt76-mt7996-add-configuration-to-suppot-wed-and-.patch
Signed-off-by: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>
[plcharriere: MT7990 TX-free mapping of the primary WED only, without the
band-1 mapping of the secondary HIF and the wlan.id assignments]
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mmio.c
+++ b/mt7996/mmio.c
@@ -661,6 +661,12 @@ int mt7996_mmio_wed_init(struct mt7996_d
 						 MT_RXQ_RING_BASE(0) +
 						 MT7996_RXQ_TXFREE0 * MT_RING_SIZE;
 			wed->wlan.txfree_tbit = ffs(MT_INT_RX_TXFREE_MAIN) - 1;
+		} else if (is_mt7990(&dev->mt76)) {
+			wed->wlan.wpdma_txfree = wed->wlan.phy_base +
+						 MT_RXQ_RING_BASE(0) +
+						 MT7990_RXQ_TXFREE0 * MT_RING_SIZE;
+			wed->wlan.txfree_tbit =
+				ffs(MT_INT_RX_TXFREE_BAND0_MT7990) - 1;
 		} else {
 			wed->wlan.txfree_tbit = ffs(MT_INT_RX_DONE_WA_MAIN) - 1;
 			wed->wlan.wpdma_txfree = wed->wlan.phy_base +
